{"from": "site:taybeh", "type": "identified_as", "to": "place:ephraim", "note": "Identified with ancient Ophrah of Benjamin (SWP 1882, backed by prominent scholars since) and traditionally with John's Ephraim (Eusebius, Onomasticon 458, via Ephron 418); the identification is a modern-tradition proposal, not certain (grade D on the attests edge)."}
{"from": "claim:jn-11-02-mary-anointed", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:jn-12-03-mary-anoints-feet-nard", "note": "John 11:2 anticipates the anointing of John 12:3, where Mary anoints his feet with nard and wipes them with her hair - the same event John defers to chapter 12."}
{"from": "claim:jn-11-43-44-raising", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:jn-12-01-lazarus-raised-in-bethany", "note": "John 12:1 presupposes the raising of John 11:43-44 (Lazarus, who had been raised, at the Bethany supper)."}
